title: The Recession Under Labour
tags: event
view-if: con_in_government = 0 and defeated_once = 1 and time >= 26 and time <= 36 and unemployment >= 6.5
max-visits: 1
new-page: true
on-arrival: labour_credibility -= 4; lab_leader_rating -= 3
face-image: img/events/two_million.jpg

= The Recession Under Labour

The second oil shock and the world recession have reached Britain, and they have reached it on Labour's watch. Unemployment is rising towards two million, factories are closing in the Midlands, and the government's answer is another round of pay talks with the TUC.

- @attack_record: Labour still isn't working.
- @recovery_plan: Offer a plan for recovery.

@attack_record
subtitle: Skilled workers listen. The wets think we sound heartless.
on-arrival: c2_con += 2*(1-dissent); labour_credibility -= 3; wet_dissent += 2

The posters go back up: the dole queue, longer this time, and the same three words. Saatchi's men say the line has never had more truth in it.

@recovery_plan
subtitle: -1 resource. The middle classes are reassured.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Requires 1 resource.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; c1_con += 2*(1-dissent); ab_con += 1*(1-dissent); wet_dissent -= 2; dry_dissent += 1

Sir Geoffrey Howe launches the Conservatives' recovery plan: lower taxes, sound money, and an end to the subsidies for industries that can't pay their way.

@sterling_labour
title: The Pound Under Pressure
tags: event
view-if: con_in_government = 0 and defeated_once = 1 and time >= 30 and time <= 48 and inflation >= 12 and sterling_labour_seen = 0
max-visits: 1
new-page: true
on-arrival: sterling_labour_seen = 1; labour_credibility -= 8; lab_leader_rating -= 4; c1_con += 1; ab_con += 1
face-image: img/events/bank_1983.jpg

= The Pound Under Pressure

With inflation back in double figures, the pound is falling and the Bank of England is spending its reserves to hold it. The Treasury talks of another approach to the International Monetary Fund. [+ prime_minister +] insists the country is not in crisis, which nobody has said since 1979 without regretting it.

- @demand_election: Demand a general election.
- @cross_party: Offer cross-party talks on the economy.

@demand_election
subtitle: The party loves it. The country is not sure.
on-arrival: thatcher_rating += 1; right_dissent -= 2; loyalist_dissent -= 2

You tell the Commons that a government that has lost control of the currency has lost the right to govern. The headlines are good; the government doesn't fall.

@cross_party
subtitle: The wets approve. The dries call it consensus politics.
on-arrival: wet_dissent -= 4; dry_dissent += 4; c1_con += 1*(1-dissent); economic_liberalism -= 1

You offer to talk. [+ prime_minister +] declines, but the offer makes you look like a Prime Minister in waiting.

@labour_left_revolt
title: Labour's Left Revolts
tags: event
view-if: con_in_government = 0 and defeated_once = 1 and time >= 38 and time <= 54 and labour_left_revolt_seen = 0
max-visits: 1
new-page: true
on-arrival: labour_left_revolt_seen = 1; labour_credibility -= 5; lab_leader_rating -= 4; c1_lab -= 1; c2_lab -= 1
face-image: img/events/foot.jpg

= Labour's Left Revolts

Tony Benn and the left have won control of Labour's National Executive and its conference. They have voted to leave the Common Market, to scrap nuclear weapons and to let the party, not the Cabinet, write the next manifesto. [+ prime_minister +] says the government will ignore them. Labour's moderates say privately that it cannot.

- @court_moderates: Court Labour's moderates.
- @let_them_fight: Let Labour fight itself.

@court_moderates
subtitle: The Liberals notice. So do Labour's voters.
on-arrival: c1_con += 1*(1-dissent); c2_con += 1*(1-dissent); lib_relation -= 2; wet_dissent -= 1

You tell Labour's voters that their party has been taken from them, and that the Conservatives are the only party left that believes in a strong Britain.

@let_them_fight
on-arrival: labour_credibility -= 2

You say nothing, and let Labour's conference speak for itself.

@falklands_labour
title: The Falklands Under Labour
tags: event
view-if: con_in_government = 0 and defeated_once = 1 and time >= 52 and time <= 56 and falklands_labour_seen = 0
max-visits: 1
new-page: true
on-arrival: {!
Q.falklands_labour_seen = 1;
// Labour sends a task force; whether it succeeds is a matter of luck and preparation
Q.falklands_labour_won = (Math.random() < 0.6) ? 1 : 0;
!}
face-image: img/events/hermes_1982.jpg

= The Falklands Under Labour

Argentina has invaded the Falkland Islands. [+ prime_minister +] has sent a task force to the South Atlantic and promises that the islands will be British again. As Leader of the Opposition, you must decide what to say.

- @back_task_force: Back the task force without reservation.
- @demand_inquiry: Back the task force, and demand to know how it happened.

@back_task_force
subtitle: Patriotic and generous. The credit goes to the government.
on-arrival: thatcher_rating += 3; right_dissent -= 3; lab_leader_rating += 4 if falklands_labour_won = 1; lab_leader_rating -= 6 if falklands_labour_won = 0

[? if falklands_labour_won = 1 : The islands are retaken in June. The government gets the credit, and you get the respect of having stood beside it. ?][? if falklands_labour_won = 0 : The task force is turned back with heavy losses. The country is grief-stricken and furious, and you were right not to play politics with it. ?]

@demand_inquiry
subtitle: Partisan, and risky. It pays only if things go wrong.
on-arrival: thatcher_rating += 3 if falklands_labour_won = 0; thatcher_rating -= 3 if falklands_labour_won = 1; labour_credibility -= 6 if falklands_labour_won = 0; right_dissent += 2

[? if falklands_labour_won = 1 : The islands are retaken in June, and your demands for an inquiry sound petty in the hour of victory. ?][? if falklands_labour_won = 0 : The task force is turned back, and your questions about the defence cuts that invited the invasion are now the country's questions. ?]

@opposition_byelection
title: A By-Election
tags: event
view-if: con_in_government = 0 and defeated_once = 1 and in_campaign = 0 and months_since_election >= 6 and random_roll < 0.07 and opp_byelection_timer <= 0
new-page: true
on-arrival: {!
Q.opp_byelection_timer = 8;
// a Labour seat falls vacant; we take it if we are well ahead
Q.opp_byelection_gain = (Q.con_votes >= Q.lab_votes + 3 + Math.random() * 4) ? 1 : 0;
if (Q.opp_byelection_gain) {
    Q.con_mps += 1;
    Q.lab_mps -= 1;
    Q.thatcher_rating += 2;
    Q.loyalist_dissent -= 3;
} else {
    Q.thatcher_rating -= 1;
}
!}
face-image: img/events/polling_station.jpg

= A By-Election

A Labour MP has died, and there is a by-election in a marginal seat. [? if opp_byelection_gain = 1 : We take it from Labour on a big swing. The government's majority shrinks again, and the papers say you are the next Prime Minister. ?][? if opp_byelection_gain = 0 : Labour holds on. Our candidate does well, but not well enough, and the knives come out again at Westminster. ?]
